# The repo-root build context is used by logos/logos-orchestrator/Dockerfile,
# logos/logos-agent/Dockerfile, logos/logos-agent/workspace/Dockerfile,
# AND iris/Dockerfile (docker-context: . in iris_build-and-push-docker.yml).
# Whitelist exactly what those Dockerfiles COPY so the context stays small
# and untracked local files (benchmarks, calibration data, .git, …) never
# get uploaded to the builder.
#
# A Dockerfile added here without its inputs whitelisted fails with
# "failed to compute cache key: … not found" — the path is simply absent from
# the context.
*
# Shared dependency: only the files the orchestrator's dependency layer
# installs from (metadata, declared readme, package source) — not the whole
# directory, so e.g. shared/poetry.lock churn never enters the build context.
!shared/pyproject.toml
!shared/README.md
!shared/shared
!logos/db
!logos/logos-orchestrator/pyproject.toml
!logos/logos-orchestrator/src
!logos/logos-orchestrator/tests
# Agent runner: the service package and the session-image entrypoints.
# Deliberately not the whole directory — no README, no tests in the image.
!logos/logos-agent/pyproject.toml
!logos/logos-agent/app
!logos/logos-agent/workspace/run_session.py
!logos/logos-agent/workspace/screenshot.js
# The model gateway's nginx configuration, shipped in its image rather than
# bind-mounted: a deployment copies only the compose file to its VM.
!logos/agent-gateway/nginx.conf
!iris/pyproject.toml
!iris/poetry.lock
!iris/src/iris
!iris/log_conf.yml
!iris/models
# Memiris packaging inputs only (iris installs it as a path dependency):
# pyproject + declared readme + both declared package dirs (src, tests).
# Deliberately NOT the whole tree — gitignored local secrets (.env,
# application.local.yml, llm_config.local.yml) must never enter the image.
!memiris/pyproject.toml
!memiris/README.md
!memiris/src
!memiris/tests
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
